          <p class="cs-card-sub">The &ldquo;Big Three&rdquo; PBM portals</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Plan-integrated, but owned by insurers or pharmacy chains</li>
            <li>Dense portals, heavy on benefit jargon</li>
            <li>Real cost is hard to see before filling, and tools lean toward affiliated pharmacies</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-body-text" style="margin-top: clamp(26px, 4.8vw, 48px);">
      <p>That mapped the opening. The discount cards were transparent but disconnected from the plan; the incumbent portals were connected but hard to read. MedImpact could be both, showing real, plan-specific prices across pharmacies before a member fills.</p>
    </div>
  </SectionContent>

  <hr class="cs-section-divider">

  <SectionContent title="User Research">
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>Competitor teardowns told me what the category had settled on. They could not tell me why MedImpact&rsquo;s own members hesitated or called support. For that I combined a short member survey to size the problem with follow-up conversations to understand it.</p>
      <p><strong>Member survey responses</strong> from people who had filled a prescription through their plan in the previous few months, plus <strong>follow-up conversations</strong> and daily input from Photon&rsquo;s product team, who fielded the questions members were calling in about.</p>
    </div>

    <h3 class="cs-subsection-title" style="margin-top: clamp(34px, 7.2vw, 72px);">What the Survey Told Us</h3>
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>The survey was deliberately short, focused on why members open the portal and where the pharmacy benefit gets confusing, because that is where the support calls clustered.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mi-survey-charts">
      {miSurveyCharts.map((item) => (
        <figure class="mi-pie-card">
          <h4>{item.q}</h4>
          <div class="mi-pie-row">
            <svg class="mi-pie" viewBox="0 0 180 180" role="img" aria-label={item.paths.map((p) => `${p.pct}% ${p.label}`).join(', ')}>
              {item.paths.map((p) => (<path d={p.d} fill={p.color} />))}
            </svg>
            <ul class="mi-pie-legend">
              {item.paths.map((p) => (
                <li>
                  <span class="mi-pie-dot" style={`background:${p.color}`} />
                  <span class="mi-pie-pct">{p.pct}%</span>
                  <span class="mi-pie-label">{p.label}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="cs-body-text" style="margin-top: clamp(26px, 4.8vw, 48px);">
      <p>Two numbers reframed the project. <strong>46% said the hardest part was knowing what a drug would cost before filling</strong>, and <strong>42% came to the portal mainly to check a price</strong>. Members were not asking for more features. Cost was the reason they showed up, and the portal was making them guess.</p>
    </div>

    <h3 class="cs-subsection-title" style="margin-top: clamp(40px, 9.6vw, 96px);">What We Asked in Interviews</h3>
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>The survey said where members struggled. The conversations said why. I kept the questions behavioral, asking what people actually did last time rather than what they think of the product.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="cs-research-questions">
      <li>Walk me through the last time you filled a prescription. How did you decide where?</li>
      <li>Before you fill, do you know what it will cost? How do you find out?</li>
      <li>When was the last time you looked at your benefits, and what were you trying to figure out?</li>
      <li>How do you keep track of refills for yourself or your family?</li>
      <li>What do you handle on your phone versus a computer?</li>
    </ol>

    <h3 class="cs-subsection-title" style="margin-top: clamp(40px, 9.6vw, 96px);">What They Told Us</h3>
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>Different words, same handful of frustrations, and each one maps to a theme that came out of the affinity map.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-research-quotes">
      <figure class="cs-research-quote">
        <blockquote>I never know what a drug is going to cost until I&rsquo;m standing at the counter.</blockquote>
        <figcaption><span>Plan member</span><em>Cost transparency</em></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cs-research-quote">
        <blockquote>I have three prescriptions and I can never remember which one is due for a refill.</blockquote>
        <figcaption><span>Plan member</span><em>Managing prescriptions</em></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cs-research-quote">
        <blockquote>I just use whatever pharmacy is closest. I didn&rsquo;t know I could compare prices.</blockquote>
        <figcaption><span>Plan member</span><em>Where to fill</em></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </SectionContent>

  <hr class="cs-section-divider">

  <SectionContent title="Key Findings">
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>The design was informed by the plan tasks themselves and by daily input from Photon's product team, who had visibility into where members had difficulty and what generated support calls. Several patterns were consistent:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Not knowing a drug's cost in advance was the most common reason members hesitated.</li>
        <li>Information shown without explanation was more likely to prompt a support call than an action.</li>
        <li>Members tended to scan rather than read, so long blocks of plan text were often skipped.</li>
        <li>A significant portion of members used the portal only on mobile.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </SectionContent>

  <hr class="cs-section-divider">

  <SectionContent title="Affinity Mapping">
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>We gathered notes from member interviews, Photon&rsquo;s support-call input, and early usability tests, then grouped them to find the patterns.</p>
      <p>Members described their frustrations differently, but the underlying themes were consistent. Whether they were talking about cost, refills, or benefits, the same questions kept surfacing.</p>
      <p>Once we clustered everything, it became clear: we weren&rsquo;t just solving for layout. We were solving for a member being able to answer &ldquo;what will this cost, and what do I do next?&rdquo;</p>
    </div>

    <h3 class="cs-subsection-title">Common Themes We Found</h3>
    <div class="cs-themes-grid">
      <div class="cs-theme">
        <h4><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 5H3" /><path d="M12 19H3" /><path d="M14 3v4" /><path d="M16 17v4" /><path d="M21 12h-9" /><path d="M21 19h-5" /><path d="M21 5h-7" /><path d="M8 10v4" /><path d="M8 12H3" /></svg>Cost transparency</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>"I never know what it&rsquo;ll cost until I pay."</li>
          <li>"Is there a cheaper version of this drug?"</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-theme">
        <h4><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 3h5v5" /><path d="M8 3H3v5" /><path d="M12 22v-8.3a4 4 0 0 0-1.172-2.872L3 3" /><path d="m15 9 6-6" /></svg>Managing prescriptions</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>"Which refill is due next?"</li>
          <li>"Can I set this to fill automatically?"</li>
          <li>"Where&rsquo;s my order right now?"</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-theme">
        <h4><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="8" height="4" x="8" y="2" rx="1" ry="1" /><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2" /><path d="m9 14 2 2 4-4" /></svg>Understanding benefits</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>"How much of my deductible is left?"</li>
          <li>"Is this drug even covered?"</li>
          <li>"What tier is it, and why?"</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-theme">
        <h4><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="6" cy="19" r="3" /><path d="M9 19h8.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0-7h-11a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0-7H15" /><circle cx="18" cy="5" r="3" /></svg>Mobile first</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>"I check this on my phone, not a computer."</li>
          <li>"The dose reminder is the main thing I use."</li>
          <li>"I want to handle it all from the app."</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="cs-subsection-title"><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5" /><path d="M9 18h6" /><path d="M10 22h4" /></svg>What This Told Us</h3>
    <p class="cs-body-text">Members didn&rsquo;t want more features. They wanted to know what things cost and what to do next, before they committed. So every design decision from here on &mdash; plan-specific prices, a savings calculator, inline refill status, plain-language benefits &mdash; was built to answer one question: &ldquo;What will this cost me, and what should I do?&rdquo;</p>

    <div class="cs-image-full">
      <img src="/images/bm-affinity-map.png" alt="Affinity map grouping member notes into themes">
    </div>

  </SectionContent>

  <hr class="cs-section-divider">

  <SectionContent title="Feature Prioritization">
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>Before grouping features, I ran a prioritization session with Photon\'s product team in Figma. Each participant worked on their own card and answered, for the dashboard, why members open it, what features would make it better, what they think about while using it, and how they feel. We then ranked the features together.</p>
    </div>

    <h4 class="mi-fp-label">What we ranked, most important first</h4>
    <ol class="mi-fp-rank">
      <li>Prescription Info</li>
      <li>Benefit Info</li>
      <li>Pricing / Savings</li>
      <li>Profile / Account Info</li>
      <li>Medicine Chest</li>
      <li>Dependant Info</li>
      <li>Claim Info</li>
      <li>Settings</li>
      <li>Billing</li>
      <li>My Profile</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="mi-fp-themes">
      <div class="mi-fp-theme"><h4>Why they open it</h4><p>Order a refill, see what a drug will cost, check when they can fill next, handle early-fill and mail-order questions, see what to take today, and manage prescriptions for dependents.</p></div>
      <div class="mi-fp-theme"><h4>Features they asked for</h4><p>Order from the dashboard, show cost and benefit tiers, ready-to-ship dates, pill and refill reminders, a to-do list, and drag-and-drop customization to show or hide modules.</p></div>
      <div class="mi-fp-theme"><h4>What they think about</h4><p>How much they have paid and how much is left on the deductible, when they can refill, whether they took their meds today, and whether a drug is covered.</p></div>
      <div class="mi-fp-theme"><h4>How they feel</h4><p>Anxious about paying for medications and stressed about pharmacy trips; frustrated when information is scattered or out of order; reassured when the deductible limit is close.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="cs-subsection-title" style="margin-top: clamp(34px, 7.2vw, 72px);">The Session Boards</h3>
    <div class="cs-body-text"><p>The prioritization matrix and each participant's notes from the live Figma session.</p></div>
    <img class="mi-fp-board" src="/images/medimpact/feature-prioritization/fp-1.png" alt="Feature prioritization ranking matrix" width="3632" height="1714" loading="lazy" />
    <div class="mi-fp-grid">
      <img src="/images/medimpact/feature-prioritization/fp-7.png" alt="Session rules and instructions" width="1616" height="1130" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/images/medimpact/feature-prioritization/fp-2.png" alt="Participant session card" width="2120" height="2842" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/images/medimpact/feature-prioritization/fp-3.png" alt="Participant session card" width="2120" height="2010" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/images/medimpact/feature-prioritization/fp-4.png" alt="Participant session card" width="2120" height="2042" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/images/medimpact/feature-prioritization/fp-5.png" alt="Participant session card" width="2120" height="1978" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/images/medimpact/feature-prioritization/fp-6.png" alt="Participant session card" width="2120" height="2586" loading="lazy" />
    </div>

    <h3 class="cs-subsection-title" style="margin-top: clamp(34px, 7.2vw, 72px);">What made the cut</h3>
    <div class="cs-problems-grid">
      <div class="cs-problem-card cs-card--green">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" /><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4" /></svg>Must-have</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Drug Price Check with plan-specific pricing</li>
          <li>My Prescriptions and refills in one place</li>
          <li>A dashboard focused on the next task</li>
          <li>Claims History with search and filters</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-problem-card cs-card--yellow">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.525 2.295a.53.53 0 0 1 .95 0l2.31 4.679a2.123 2.123 0 0 0 1.595 1.16l5.166.756a.53.53 0 0 1 .294.904l-3.736 3.638a2.123 2.123 0 0 0-.611 1.878l.882 5.14a.53.53 0 0 1-.771.56l-4.618-2.428a2.122 2.122 0 0 0-1.973 0L6.396 21.01a.53.53 0 0 1-.77-.56l.881-5.139a2.122 2.122 0 0 0-.611-1.879L2.16 9.795a.53.53 0 0 1 .294-.906l5.165-.755a2.122 2.122 0 0 0 1.597-1.16z" /></svg>Nice-to-have</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Vaccine recommendations and scheduling</li>
          <li>Savings calculator and mail-order comparison</li>
          <li>Dependent and profile switching</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-problem-card cs-card--red">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" /><path d="M4.929 4.929 19.07 19.071" /></svg>Not in this release</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>A full plan-selection wizard beyond benefit highlights</li>
          <li>Provider- or pharmacy-side tools</li>
          <li>Features that depended on data the plan could not yet provide</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </SectionContent>

  <hr class="cs-section-divider">

  <SectionContent title="User Flows">
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>These are the main tasks a member comes to the portal to do. Each flow starts from the dashboard and ends where the task is done, so the whole path is visible in one place.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mi-flows-list">
      {miFlows.map((f, idx) => (
        <div class="cs-subsection" style={idx > 0 ? "margin-top: clamp(26px, 4.8vw, 48px);" : undefined}>
          <h3 class="cs-subsection-title">{f.title}</h3>
          <div class="cs-flow-pills">
            {f.pills.map((p) => <span set:html={p} />)}
          </div>
          <div class="cs-body-text">
            <p>{f.note}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-image-full" style="margin-top: 26px;" set:html={miFlowSvgs[idx]} />
        </div>
      ))}
      <p style="margin: 28px 0 4px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #888; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Legend</p>
      <div class="cs-image-full" style="max-width: 620px; margin-left: 0; margin-top: 6px;" set:html={miflowLegend} />
    </div>
  </SectionContent>

  <hr class="cs-section-divider">

  <SectionContent title="The Solution">
    <div class="cs-body-text">
      <p>The redesign is organized around member tasks. Each area of the portal addresses a specific need.</p>
      <h3>Summary of changes</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-problems-grid" style="margin-top: 24px;">
      <div class="cs-problem-card">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="20" height="12" x="2" y="6" rx="2" /><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2" /><path d="M6 12h.01M18 12h.01" /></svg>Drug price comparison</h3>
        <p>Drug Price Check displays plan-specific costs across pharmacies, with mail order and local pickup shown together, so members can compare before filling.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-problem-card">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="8" height="4" x="8" y="2" rx="1" ry="1" /><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2" /><path d="M12 11h4" /><path d="M12 16h4" /><path d="M8 11h.01" /><path d="M8 16h.01" /></svg>Consolidated prescriptions</h3>
        <p>Active prescriptions, refill status, and auto-refill settings are shown in one place.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-problem-card">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="7" height="9" x="3" y="3" rx="1" /><rect width="7" height="5" x="14" y="3" rx="1" /><rect width="7" height="9" x="14" y="12" rx="1" /><rect width="7" height="5" x="3" y="16" rx="1" /></svg>Task-focused dashboard</h3>
        <p>The dashboard shows to-do items, savings, and prescription status on the first screen.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-problem-card">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m21 21-4.34-4.34" /><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" /></svg>Searchable claims</h3>
        <p>Claims history can be filtered by drug, pharmacy, physician, and date, with active filters shown as removable pills.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-problem-card">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m18 2 4 4" /><path d="m17 7 3-3" /><path d="M19 9 8.7 19.3c-1 1-2.5 1-3.4 0l-.6-.6c-1-1-1-2.5 0-3.4L15 5" /><path d="m9 11 4 4" /><path d="m5 19-3 3" /><path d="m14 4 6 6" /></svg>Guided vaccine and enrollment flows</h3>
        <p>The vaccine and open enrollment modules were built as step-by-step flows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-problem-card">
        <h3><svg class="cs-ico" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="10" height="14" x="3" y="8" rx="2" /><path d="M5 4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h12a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-2.4" /><path d="M8 18h.01" /></svg>Mobile parity</h3>
        <p>Each task was designed for mobile as well as desktop.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </SectionContent>

  <hr class="cs-section-divider">

<SectionContent title="Stylized UI Components">
    {miComponents.map((c, i) => (
      <div class="cs-component-showcase" style={i > 0 ? 'margin-top: clamp(44px, 12vw, 120px);' : ''}>
